==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈkɒk.ˌl/}}
* {{rhymes|ɒkəl}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|fro}} ''[[cokille]]'' (French ''[[coquille]]''), from {{etyl|la}} ''*cocchilia'', form of ''[[conchylia]]'', from {{etyl|grc}} '''{{polytonic|[[κογχύλιον]]}}''' (konkhylion), diminutive of '''{{polytonic|[[κογχύλη]]}}''' ‘mussel’.

====Noun====
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# Any of various [[edible]] [[European]] [[bivalve]] [[mollusk]]s, of the [[family]] ''[[Cardiidae]]'', having [[heart]]-[[shaped]] [[shell]]s.
# The [[shel]]l of such cockle.
# (''plural'') One’s [[innermost]] [[feeling]]s (only in the expression “[[warm the cockles of one's heart|the cockles of one’s heart]]”).
# [''directly from French coquille''] A [[wrinkle]], [[pucker]]
# ''hence'' A defect in [[sheepskin]]; firm dark [[nodule]]s caused by the bites of [[ked]]s on live sheep

